WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.720 --> 00:00:04.240
Zooey Deschanel has been largely&nbsp;
absent from our screens over the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.240 --> 00:00:08.400
past couple of years - but happily,&nbsp;
it's for several solid reasons.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:09.120 --> 00:00:13.804
Here's why you haven't seen Zooey&nbsp;
Deschanel in TV or movies as much lately.

00:00:14.560 --> 00:00:20.720
From 2011 to 2018, Zooey Deschanel starred as&nbsp;
Jessica Day - a sweet, quirky teacher who moves&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:20.720 --> 00:00:26.480
in with three strangers in Los Angeles after a&nbsp;
terrible breakup -- on the hit comedy New Girl.

00:00:26.480 --> 00:00:28.087
"Who’s Jess?"

00:00:28.087 --> 00:00:31.520
Though the role netted her Emmy&nbsp;
and Golden Globe nominations,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:31.520 --> 00:00:34.400
it may have also pigeonholed her as a performer.

00:00:34.400 --> 00:00:39.760
There's no question that Jess and Deschanel share&nbsp;
a lot of traits, from their musical talents to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:39.760 --> 00:00:45.680
their love of vintage clothing, and early seasons&nbsp;
of New Girl really leaned on those similarities.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:45.680 --> 00:00:50.720
The show sharpened a bit in later seasons,&nbsp;
and even poked fun at Jess's highly manicured&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:50.720 --> 00:00:56.960
quirkiness. Unfortunately, if you didn't invest in&nbsp;
New Girl longterm, you missed all that evolution,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:56.960 --> 00:01:02.000
which potentially made her harder to cast in&nbsp;
roles that differed too drastically from Jess.

00:01:02.880 --> 00:01:07.920
Between her leading role on New Girl and her&nbsp;
starring turn alongside Joseph Gordon-Levitt&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:07.920 --> 00:01:13.520
in 500 Days of Summer, the fact is that many of&nbsp;
Deschanel's most high-profile characters fit the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:13.520 --> 00:01:20.080
definition of the "Manic Pixie Dream Girl." A term&nbsp;
coined by critic Nathan Rabin after he saw Cameron&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:20.080 --> 00:01:23.520
Crowe's 2005 film Elizabethtown - specifically,&nbsp;
to address Kirsten Dunst's character - it became&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:23.520 --> 00:01:26.160
a catchall phrase for quirky female characters,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:26.160 --> 00:01:31.280
and unfortunately, Deschanel fit the&nbsp;
stereotype to a T, at least superficially.

00:01:31.280 --> 00:01:36.800
For example, 500 Days of Summer's leading&nbsp;
lady, Summer, could best be described as a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:36.800 --> 00:01:41.440
Manic Pixie Dream Girl by detractors who&nbsp;
would prefer to ignore the depths of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:41.440 --> 00:01:45.600
character — as well as the strength of&nbsp;
Deschanel's performance - diminishing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:45.600 --> 00:01:50.720
Summer to a girl who loves vintage clothes,&nbsp;
is tweely eccentric, and who encourages the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:50.720 --> 00:01:56.640
film's male protagonist to make big choices in&nbsp;
his life. Rabin ultimately apologized for even&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:56.640 --> 00:02:01.760
creating the concept of a Manic Pixie Dream&nbsp;
Girl years later, but the popularity of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:01.760 --> 00:02:06.640
trope - and its backlash - may have affected&nbsp;
Deschanel's opportunities in Hollywood.

00:02:07.625 --> 00:02:12.080
Plenty of actors have moved into producing while&nbsp;
still appearing in front of the camera - even&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:12.080 --> 00:02:17.840
megawatt stars like Brad Pitt, who actually won&nbsp;
his first Academy Award for producing 12 Years&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:17.840 --> 00:02:24.160
a Slave several years before he won a competitive&nbsp;
Oscar for acting. Zooey Deschanel is no different.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:24.160 --> 00:02:30.480
In fact, she moved behind the camera on New Girl&nbsp;
during its run. In 2011, she became a producer,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:30.480 --> 00:02:36.468
and from 2014 until the show ended in&nbsp;
2018, also served as an executive producer.

00:02:36.468 --> 00:02:41.490
Deschanel also ventured into producing some&nbsp;
other projects throughout her run on New Girl.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:41.490 --> 00:02:44.400
Even if she isn't appearing&nbsp;
onscreen, in other words,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:44.400 --> 00:02:49.710
there's always a chance Deschanel could produce&nbsp;
again if the right project catches her eye.

00:02:49.710 --> 00:02:54.640
Aside from her acting career, one of Zooey&nbsp;
Deschanel's longtime passion projects&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:54.640 --> 00:02:57.920
has been promoting vegan and vegetarian lifestyles&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:57.920 --> 00:03:03.280
while helping consumers understand where their&nbsp;
food actually comes from. For multiple seasons,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:03.280 --> 00:03:07.920
Deschanel has hosted the webseries Your&nbsp;
Food's Roots, where she talks to farmers,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:07.920 --> 00:03:13.600
nutritionists, food historians, and other&nbsp;
experts about how the food you choose affects you&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:13.600 --> 00:03:17.760
as well as the people around you, larger&nbsp;
communities, and the Earth as a whole.

00:03:17.760 --> 00:03:23.120
In fact, working on the show encouraged&nbsp;
Deschanel to become a vegetarian to adopt&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:23.120 --> 00:03:28.080
more ethical food practices. As she once&nbsp;
explained to People magazine, she learned&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:28.080 --> 00:03:33.120
so much about where her food was really coming&nbsp;
from, that she began paying more attention.

00:03:33.120 --> 00:03:36.720
"The main thing is it's just so hard&nbsp;
to know where meat is coming from.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:36.720 --> 00:03:41.600
It's so difficult to know if it was sustainably&nbsp;
raised [or] humanely raised. I really felt like&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:41.600 --> 00:03:46.080
I couldn't be sure where it was coming from&nbsp;
most of the time. So I stopped eating meat."

00:03:46.960 --> 00:03:52.560
Near the height of her career momentum in 2011,&nbsp;
Zooey Deschanel found time to create a place for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:52.560 --> 00:03:59.760
women of all ages online. Alongside co-founders&nbsp;
Molly McAleer and Sophia Rossi, Deschanel founded&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:59.760 --> 00:04:05.600
HelloGiggles just as she landed her starring role&nbsp;
on New Girl. According to HelloGiggles itself,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:05.600 --> 00:04:11.440
the site is meant to serve as a, quote, "positive&nbsp;
online community for female-identifying readers,"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:11.440 --> 00:04:15.440
and covers everything from beauty&nbsp;
to relationship to finance.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:15.440 --> 00:04:21.200
To do this, the site combines personal&nbsp;
essays with news, lists, and columns.

00:04:21.200 --> 00:04:28.240
In 2015, Deschanel, McAleer, and Rossi sold&nbsp;
HelloGiggles to Time Inc., but still continued&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:28.240 --> 00:04:34.160
overseeing the website as it gained an even wider&nbsp;
audience. As Deschanel told the Los Angeles Times&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:34.160 --> 00:04:39.040
in a statement, the purchase meant the trio and&nbsp;
their staff would be able to reach an even wider&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:39.040 --> 00:04:44.548
audience through the resources offered by Time.&nbsp;
HelloGiggles is still around to do that today.

00:04:45.280 --> 00:04:51.120
In 2015, Zooey Deschanel took on one of the&nbsp;
most important roles of her life - becoming&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:51.120 --> 00:04:57.680
a mother - with the birth of her first child,&nbsp;
daughter Elsie Wolf. In 2017, with then-husband&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:57.680 --> 00:05:03.440
Jacob Pechenik, she had a son, Charlie&nbsp;
Wolf, before the couple parted ways in 2019.

00:05:03.440 --> 00:05:08.640
In 2018, Deschanel told InStyle that&nbsp;
she was in no rush to return to acting,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:08.640 --> 00:05:10.800
preferring to focus on her children.

00:05:10.800 --> 00:05:15.600
"I'm just looking for something that would be&nbsp;
exciting and fulfilling for me. I have two kids,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:15.600 --> 00:05:18.720
and they're very important to&nbsp;
me. I'm really focused on them,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:18.720 --> 00:05:21.200
so I want to make sure that whatever I do next&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:21.200 --> 00:05:25.840
is really good. It has to be really good&nbsp;
for me to leave them [and go to work]."

00:05:25.840 --> 00:05:31.680
By Deschanel's own admission, she's also a&nbsp;
very hands-on parent, as she also told InStyle

00:05:31.680 --> 00:05:37.040
"I mean, I'm driving my kids to every class,&nbsp;
every day. I'm there with them all the time.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:37.040 --> 00:05:42.000
It's actually rare that I'm not with them. I&nbsp;
try to be there as much as humanly possible."

00:05:42.800 --> 00:05:47.920
Ever since New Girl ended in 2018, audiences&nbsp;
haven't seen Zooey Deschanel onscreen&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:47.920 --> 00:05:53.440
in an acting role. But if you listen closely&nbsp;
to some recent - and huge - children's movies,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:53.440 --> 00:05:58.240
you'll be able to hear her distinctive&nbsp;
voice. Live-action acting might be on hold,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:58.240 --> 00:06:01.760
but voice acting is still a part&nbsp;
of Deschanel's working life.

00:06:01.760 --> 00:06:07.200
In 2016, Deschanel began appearing in the&nbsp;
enormously successful Trolls franchise,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:07.200 --> 00:06:11.840
voicing Bridget, a member of the&nbsp;
antagonistic Bergen race. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:11.840 --> 00:06:17.280
Bridget is a particularly sweet Bergen, harboring&nbsp;
a secret crush on the Prince of the Bergens,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:17.280 --> 00:06:21.120
Gristle Jr., and working as a&nbsp;
scullery maid in the palace.

00:06:21.601 --> 00:06:26.720
"You love Gristle, too? You&nbsp;
better back off, girlfriend."

00:06:26.720 --> 00:06:32.080
After the first film, Deschanel returned not&nbsp;
only for the much-anticipated 2020 sequel&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:32.080 --> 00:06:36.560
Trolls World Tour, which marked&nbsp;
her first acting gig since 2017,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:36.560 --> 00:06:42.080
but she also appeared in NBC's Trolls Holiday&nbsp;
special, reprising her role as Bridget in both&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:42.080 --> 00:06:47.200
projects. Whether it's to cater to her children&nbsp;
or just because voice work is a fun gig for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:47.200 --> 00:06:52.000
major actors to play with, Deschanel is clearly&nbsp;
doing well with her work in the Trolls movies.

00:06:52.800 --> 00:06:58.000
Even throughout the highest highs of her film&nbsp;
and television career, Zooey Deschanel always&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:58.000 --> 00:07:04.800
kept her true passion project, the band She &amp;&nbsp;
Him, alive. Alongside partner M. Ward, the duo&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:04.800 --> 00:07:11.680
has released several albums, and with Deschanel&nbsp;
on piano, vocals, and ukulele and Ward on guitar,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:11.680 --> 00:07:16.640
the two strike a decidedly folksy sound.&nbsp;
They've been quite successful, releasing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:16.640 --> 00:07:24.240
2008's Volume One, 2010's Volume Two, 2013's&nbsp;
Volume Three and A Very She &amp; Him Christmas,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:24.240 --> 00:07:28.400
2014's Classics, and 2016's Christmas Party.

00:07:28.400 --> 00:07:35.040
Between albums, Ward and Deschanel also play live;&nbsp;
as recently as 2019, the two were still doing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:35.040 --> 00:07:40.400
holiday tours, visiting several cities during&nbsp;
the season to spread musical cheer. In fact,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:40.400 --> 00:07:45.760
during their 2019 Christmas Party tour, Deschanel&nbsp;
was spotted bringing her famous boyfriend,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:45.760 --> 00:07:50.800
Property Brother Jonathan Scott, on stage&nbsp;
during a show at the Met in Philadelphia.

00:07:51.680 --> 00:07:58.800
After meeting during a taping of Carpool&nbsp;
Karaoke in 2019, Zooey Deschanel and HGTV star&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:58.800 --> 00:08:04.000
and Property Brother Jonathan Scott started&nbsp;
dating, and over time, the two slowly made&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:04.000 --> 00:08:09.440
their relationship public. Throughout several&nbsp;
cute Instagram posts and other milestones,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:09.440 --> 00:08:12.880
Deschanel and Scott have opened&nbsp;
up about their relationship,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:12.880 --> 00:08:18.880
and in December of 2020, Deschanel put in an&nbsp;
appearance alongside Scott on his home network.

00:08:18.880 --> 00:08:25.280
Deschanel appeared in an episode of the HGTV&nbsp;
series Celebrity IOU, which sees celebrities&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:25.280 --> 00:08:30.880
do special construction and renovations favors&nbsp;
for friends and loved ones via the hosting and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:30.880 --> 00:08:36.800
producing powers of the Property Brothers. In this&nbsp;
sweet installment, Deschanel helps out a longtime&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:36.800 --> 00:08:42.400
friend - Sarah, who has been a part of her life&nbsp;
since kindergarten — by expanding her home into&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:42.400 --> 00:08:47.760
an open-space concept. Beyond Deschanel's&nbsp;
amazing gesture, it's even cuter knowing that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:47.760 --> 00:08:52.720
she's appearing alongside Scott, her real-life&nbsp;
partner, and supporting his television ventures.

00:08:53.734 --> 00:08:57.360
Zooey Deschanel's blunt bangs,&nbsp;
"adorkable" personality,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:57.360 --> 00:09:02.080
and ukulele-fueled indie band have&nbsp;
made her an easily spoofable celebrity&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:02.080 --> 00:09:07.520
over the years. Now that she's out of the&nbsp;
spotlight, Deschanel is poking fun at herself,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:07.520 --> 00:09:13.040
and even appeared in a music video alongside&nbsp;
Katy Perry to reference a long-running joke.

00:09:13.040 --> 00:09:16.800
There's no denying that Deschanel&nbsp;
and Perry look eerily similar,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:16.800 --> 00:09:21.120
to the point where Perry even admitted&nbsp;
that she occasionally pretended to be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:21.120 --> 00:09:28.000
Deschanel to gain access to exclusive events&nbsp;
and clubs. Finally, in December of 2020, the duo&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:28.000 --> 00:09:32.960
made light of their similarity when Deschanel&nbsp;
starred in the music video for Perry's song&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:32.960 --> 00:09:37.680
"Not the End of the World," one of the&nbsp;
singles from her Smile album. In the video,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:37.680 --> 00:09:43.760
Deschanel plays an unsuspecting human who finds&nbsp;
herself held captive by aliens who really,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:43.760 --> 00:09:49.440
really like Katy Perry, and even try to get&nbsp;
Deschanel's character to perform as the pop&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:49.440 --> 00:09:55.760
star. It's a bit that perfectly capitalizes on the&nbsp;
constant claims that the two stars are lookalikes.

